---
title: ActionGroup
description:
  Groups related actions in a row or stack and optionally supports selection.
category: Buttons
---

## Example

```jsx {% live=true %}
let [action, setAction] = React.useState();

return (
  <Flex direction="column" gap="large" alignItems="start">
    <ActionGroup aria-label="Actions" onAction={setAction}>
      <ActionGroupItem id="add">Add</ActionGroupItem>
      <ActionGroupItem id="edit">Edit</ActionGroupItem>
      <ActionGroupItem id="delete">Delete</ActionGroupItem>
    </ActionGroup>
    <Text>Action: {action}</Text>
  </Flex>
);
```

## Collections

`ActionGroup` uses explicit `ActionGroupItem` children. Dynamic data is
provided with `items` and a render function.

```jsx {% live=true %}
let items = [
  { id: 'add', label: 'Add' },
  { id: 'edit', label: 'Edit' },
  { id: 'delete', label: 'Delete' },
];

return (
  <ActionGroup
    aria-label="Actions"
    items={items}
    onAction={key => alert(key)}
  >
    {item => <ActionGroupItem id={item.id}>{item.label}</ActionGroupItem>}
  </ActionGroup>
);
```

## Icons

```jsx {% live=true %}
<ActionGroup aria-label="Actions">
  <ActionGroupItem id="add" textValue="Add">
    <Icon src={plusIcon} />
    <Text>Add</Text>
  </ActionGroupItem>
  <ActionGroupItem id="edit" textValue="Edit">
    <Icon src={editIcon} />
    <Text>Edit</Text>
  </ActionGroupItem>
  <ActionGroupItem id="delete" textValue="Delete">
    <Icon src={trashIcon} />
    <Text>Delete</Text>
  </ActionGroupItem>
</ActionGroup>
```

## Selection

Use `selectionMode` for toggle-button groups. Selection can be controlled
with `selectedKeys` and `onSelectionChange`, or initialized with
`defaultSelectedKeys`.

```jsx {% live=true %}
<ActionGroup
  aria-label="Text style"
  selectionMode="multiple"
  defaultSelectedKeys={['bold']}
>
  <ActionGroupItem id="bold">Bold</ActionGroupItem>
  <ActionGroupItem id="italic">Italic</ActionGroupItem>
  <ActionGroupItem id="underline">Underline</ActionGroupItem>
</ActionGroup>
```

## Overflow

`overflowMode="wrap"` wraps actions. With `overflowMode="collapse"`, actions
that do not fit move into an explicit overflow menu. Provide a data/render
source when items need to be transformed responsively.

```jsx {% live=true %}
let actions = [
  { id: 'add', label: 'Add' },
  { id: 'edit', label: 'Edit' },
  { id: 'copy', label: 'Copy' },
  { id: 'delete', label: 'Delete' },
];

return (
  <ActionGroup
    aria-label="Actions"
    items={actions}
    overflowMode="collapse"
    maxWidth="scale.1200"
  >
    {item => <ActionGroupItem id={item.id}>{item.label}</ActionGroupItem>}
  </ActionGroup>
);
```

## Links

```jsx {% live=true %}
<ActionGroup aria-label="Websites">
  <ActionGroupItem id="keystatic" href="https://keystatic.com">
    Keystatic
  </ActionGroupItem>
  <ActionGroupItem id="keystone" href="https://keystonejs.com">
    Keystone
  </ActionGroupItem>
</ActionGroup>
```
